# Example: prod-mode invocation of config/Caddyfile.
#
# This file is NOT loaded by Caddy directly — it's a reference snippet
# referenced from doc/DEPLOY.md.  Caddy is configured by ONE Caddyfile
# (config/Caddyfile); prod vs dev is selected via env vars.
#
# What changes on prod:
#
#   ANTHIVE_LISTEN                 http://127.0.0.1:8500   (no TLS — nginx terminates)
#   ANTHIVE_TLS_SNIPPET            caddy-tls.prod          (empty snippet)
#   ANTHIVE_AUTH_SNIPPET           caddy-auth.prod         (empty — trust nginx headers)
#   ANTHIVE_HTTP_REDIRECT_SNIPPET  caddy-http-redirect.prod (empty — no :8500 redirect block)
#   ANTHIVE_CADDY_BIND             127.0.0.1               (localhost-only — nginx is in front)
#
# Equivalent shell invocation for a manual test:
#
#   cd /data/anthive/anthive4
#   ANTHIVE_LISTEN="http://127.0.0.1:8500" \
#   ANTHIVE_TLS_SNIPPET="caddy-tls.prod" \
#   ANTHIVE_AUTH_SNIPPET="caddy-auth.prod" \
#   ANTHIVE_HTTP_REDIRECT_SNIPPET="caddy-http-redirect.prod" \
#   ANTHIVE_CADDY_BIND="127.0.0.1" \
#       ./envs/caddy/caddy run --config config/Caddyfile
#
# Equivalent supervisor invocation (preferred — auto-restarts on crash):
#
#   ANTHIVE_PROD=1 ./bin/ops/ant-supervisor --caddy
#
# Equivalent systemd unit fragment (see doc/DEPLOY.md for full unit):
#
#   [Service]
#   Environment=ANTHIVE_PROD=1
#   ExecStart=/data/anthive/anthive4/bin/ops/ant-supervisor --caddy
#
# Smoke test once Caddy is up:
#
#   curl -sv http://127.0.0.1:8500/api/health -H 'Remote-User: smoke-test'
#   # → expect: HTTP/1.1 200 OK with JSON body listing databases.
#
# Confirming no TLS attempts in the log (the dev mode's `tls internal`
# stanza is OFF in prod — `caddy validate` and the startup log should
# show "HTTP/2 skipped because it requires TLS" rather than any
# certificate-management messages).
